    "readThisBeforeQuotingAnything": "No CodeQL run produced these bytes. There is no recorded CodeQL output anywhere in this repository (checked: paper_data/, security-experiment/_results/), and the CodeQL CLI is not installed on the machine this package was written on. This file was hand-written against the OASIS SARIF 2.1.0 specification and the shapes CodeQL's published documentation says it emits.",
    "contrastWith": "src/fixtures/semgrep-samples-vulnerable.json is TOOL-RECORDED (genuine Semgrep 1.165.0 bytes). The two fixtures are NOT equal evidence and must never be quoted as if they were. The Semgrep adapter is tested against a real tool's output; the CodeQL adapter is tested against a format.",
    "whatIsVerifiedByThisFixture": "That the CodeQL adapter reads SARIF 2.1.0 the way the specification says to read it: rules resolved across tool.driver and tool.extensions, level defaulted from the rule's defaultConfiguration and then from the specification's own default, percent-decoded artifact URIs, and results with no locatable region refused rather than guessed.",
    "whatIsNotVerified": "That real CodeQL emits exactly these rule ids, tag spellings, or property names. The rule ids below are taken from the published github/codeql query catalog and are UNCONFIRMED here. A wrong id can only cost coverage (a finding classifies as unmapped), never fabricate an agreement — see the weaknessClass mapping's own note.",
    "specReferences": [
      "SARIF 2.1.0 3.27.10 — result.level and its defaulting chain",
      "SARIF 2.1.0 3.19.31 / 3.52.3 — toolComponentReference, rules living in tool.extensions",
      "SARIF 2.1.0 3.4.1 — artifactLocation.uri is a URI reference, so it is percent-encoded",
      "SARIF 2.1.0 3.30.1 — originalUriBaseIds"
    ]
  },
